---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import CodeSnippet from '../components/CodeSnippet.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main class="landing">
			<section class="hero">
				<h1>Global workflows for LLM agents</h1>
				<p class="hero-copy">
					Write one protocol: who talks to whom, who calls a model, and who owns
					each decision. ZipperGen turns it into a separate program for each
					participant and runs them. Coordination deadlocks are ruled out by
					construction, and the core theorem is machine-checked in Lean 4.
				</p>
				<div class="hero-actions">
					<a class="button primary" href="https://github.com/zippergen-io/zippergen">View on GitHub</a>
					<a class="button secondary" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.17612">Read the paper</a>
					<a href="https://github.com/zippergen-io/zippergen-lean/tree/main/isola">
						<img src="/lean.svg" alt="Lean verified" height="30" />
					</a>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="peek">
				<CodeSnippet
					code={`@workflow
def email_approval() -> int:
    Mailbox: message = next_unread_message()
    while message @ Mailbox:
        Mailbox(message) >> Writer(message)
        Writer: draft = draft_reply(message)
        Writer(draft) >> Mailbox(draft)
        Mailbox: approved = approve_reply(draft)
        if approved @ Mailbox:
            Mailbox: handled = send_reply(draft, handled)
        else:
            Mailbox: handled = discard(handled)
        Mailbox: message = next_unread_message()
    return handled @ Mailbox`}
				/>
				<p class="caption">
					<code>@ Mailbox</code> says who owns the decision. The Writer is never told
					what was approved, because it does nothing either way, so the branch is
					left out of its program entirely. Nobody writes that by hand.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="closing">
				<p>
					The README, a tutorial, and the full guide are on GitHub. The
					projection is based on Message Sequence Charts and choreographic
					programming.
				</p>
				<p class="refs">
					Bollig, F&uuml;gger, Nowak. <em>Provable Coordination for LLM Agents via Message Sequence Charts.</em>
					<a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.17612">arXiv:2604.17612</a>. ISoLA 2026.
				</p>
				<p class="refs">
					Bollig. <em>Deadlock-Free Parallel Regions for Projected Workflows.</em> EXPRESS/SOS 2026.
				</p>
				<p class="refs">
					Bollig. <em>Causal Past Logic for Runtime Verification of Distributed LLM Agent Workflows.</em>
					<a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.20923">arXiv:2605.20923</a>. ICFEM 2026.
				</p>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	.landing {
		width: 100%;
		max-width: none;
		padding: 0;
		overflow-x: hidden;
	}

	.landing :global(pre) {
		margin: 0;
	}

	.hero,
	.peek,
	.closing {
		width: min(760px, calc(100% - 2rem));
		margin: 0 auto;
	}

	.hero {
		padding: 4rem 0 1.5rem;
	}

	.hero h1 {
		margin: 0 0 1rem;
		font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 2.9rem);
		line-height: 1.1;
	}

	.hero-copy {
		margin: 0 0 1.75rem;
		font-size: 1.08rem;
		line-height: 1.6;
		color: rgb(var(--gray-dark));
	}

	.hero-actions {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.75rem;
	}

	.button {
		display: inline-block;
		padding: 0.6rem 1.15rem;
		border-radius: 6px;
		font-weight: 600;
		text-decoration: none;
	}

	.button.primary {
		background: var(--accent);
		color: white;
	}

	.button.secondary {
		border: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
		color: var(--accent-dark);
	}

	.peek {
		padding: 1.5rem 0;
	}

	.caption {
		margin: 1rem 0 0;
		font-size: 0.95rem;
		line-height: 1.55;
		color: rgb(var(--gray-dark));
	}

	.closing {
		padding: 1rem 0 4rem;
		font-size: 0.95rem;
		line-height: 1.55;
		color: rgb(var(--gray-dark));
	}

	.refs {
		margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
		font-size: 0.85rem;
	}
</style>
